{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558013-dtf-lore-and-torment-rule","id":1558013,"title":"DtF: Lore and Torment Rule","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-30T02:23:43-08:00","id":1558013,"title":"DtF: Lore and Torment Rule","content":"&quot;...When you attempt to perform an evocation, compare the successes on your Faith roll against your Torment. If the successful dice all show numbers greater than your Torment, you can use the positive aspects of the power normally. If one or more of the successful dice show numbers equal to or less than your Torment score, it perverts your efforts, and you use the high-Torment aspect of the power instead...&quot;<br /> <br /> It's just my feeling, or this rule is actually bugged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T06:52:16-08:00","id":1558019,"title":"","content":"From a mechanical standpoint, what I see is that as long as Torment is lower than the difficulty threshold there is no chance of corruption. At a Torment of 10 it is literally impossible to use the low Torment version of the power. It's a little counterintuitive that lower difficulty Faith rolls are more likely to be corrupted than high difficulty ones, but I don't know that it is wrong, per se. It also means that the more successes you get the higher the chance of corruption. I don't know that either of those run counter to the themes of the game, even if they aren't ideal.<br /> <br /> I admittedly haven't done anything with Demon for a long time, though, so I don't remember how much the high Torment version of powers derail what the Demon is trying to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T09:01:19-08:00","id":1558020,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was a bit off to me, but now I think I can see where the trick is.<br /> Also it don't tell what happens if the Faith roll fails. We can assume high-torment is triggered if the roll fails?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T10:04:56-08:00","id":1558024,"title":"","content":"I think it just fails. Certainly if there are no successes, there are no successes that are equal to or less than Torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T15:26:57-08:00","id":1558032,"title":"","content":"The math probably isn't exactly what the designers were hoping for (but far from the worse in the WoD in that regard), but I do think that the goal is for Lore activation to get more risky the bigger your impact is via successes rolled. Basically the more you tap into your powers, the more the Fall can twist them.<br /> <br /> I also agree that a failed roll is a failed activation so nothing happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T08:30:26-08:00","id":1558071,"title":"","content":"I realized from reading another thread about Demon that the Players Guide gave Errata for this issue. The rule from the PG is that if the majority of successes are lower than Torment the high Torment version is used. If the majority are higher, or there is a tie, the low Torment version is used. Since it matters for calculation, 1s cancel out the highest successes first, so they push towards the high torment version or failure.<br /> <br /> This rebalances how often High Torment shows up the higher the dice pools get, though it still looks like easier rolls are more likely to be tormented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T18:44:04-07:00","id":1562214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558013-dtf-lore-and-torment-rule?p=1558019#post1558019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admittedly haven't done anything with Demon for a long time, though, so I don't remember how much the high Torment version of powers derail what the Demon is trying to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some relatively little, but for others quite a lot. For some powers High Torment adds a damage or fear effect. For other it inverts the effect completely.<br /> <br /> Torment as a score is repetitive but functional, but the actual Torment mechanics demand severe revision.<br /> <br /> So, this rule is bugged, and isn't the only one in the game, but not impossible to adapt either and far from the worse we've seen.<br /> <br /> My suggestion: have the positive versions use Torment as Diff if higher than normal Diff and call it a day. The character has a harder time making such effects with High-Torment, but won't try to heal a patient and accidentally blow their head off with a shotgun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}